<header><p class="st-kicker">crusader state · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Ibelin</h1><p class="st-meta">1141 CE – 1187 CE · capital Ibelin</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Crusader lordship whose castle gave its name to the Ibelins, the most powerful noble family of Outremer and Cyprus.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1141 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fulk-king-of-jerusalem">King Fulk</a> built a castle at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yavne">Yibna</a> (Yavne), on the coastal plain south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaffa">Jaffa</a>, as one of a ring of forts to contain the Fatimid garrison of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashkelon">Ascalon</a>. He granted it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barisan-of-ibelin">Barisan</a>, constable of Jaffa, whose descendants took the name of Ibelin.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The lordship itself was small, but the family rose quickly through marriage, gaining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramla">Ramla</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirabel-castle">Mirabel</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nablus">Nablus</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barisan-of-ibelin">Barisan</a>'s sons Hugh, Baldwin and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balian-of-ibelin">Balian of Ibelin</a> were leading barons; Balian married the dowager queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-komnene-queen-of-jerusalem">Maria Komnene</a>. The castle lost its military purpose after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashkelon">Ascalon</a> fell in 1153.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Ibelin was lost to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> in 1187, the year Balian negotiated the surrender of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. The family survived the catastrophe and in the 13th century dominated <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/beirut">Beirut</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaffa">Jaffa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsuf">Arsuf</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-cyprus">Kingdom of Cyprus</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lordship-of-ibelin.jpg" alt="Lordship of Ibelin" width="320" height="352"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blason_Royaume_de_J%C3%A9rusalem.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1141 CE – 1187 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>crusader state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ibelin</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Barisan of Ibelin, Hugh of Ibelin, Balian of Ibelin</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Latin Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/israel">Israel</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ibelin</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1164&amp;focus=lordship-of-ibelin" aria-label="Lordship of Ibelin on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5575 1018 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Ibelin lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5895 1274L5908 1277M5895 1274L5811 1337"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5908 1277h0M5811 1337h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5895 1274h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5895 1274h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ibelin. <a href="/atlas?year=1164&amp;focus=lordship-of-ibelin">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

